**How to implement.** The slot bar's state in the window model: which chip's list is open and what each chip lists (001 §J 'each dropdown lists compatible items only; choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one'; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message). The bar that shows it is step 280's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `slotChipOpenOpt : Library.ElementId option`, the slot whose chip's list is open, with a one-line doc; `initWith` sets it to `None`. (2) On the model extension holding `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263): `member model.slotChipItems (slot : Setups.SetupSlot) : Item list` is `slot.fittingItems model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 277), what that slot's chip lists. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ToggleSlotChip of Library.ElementId`, with a one-line doc: open that slot's chip list, or close it when it is the open one. Its arm writes nothing, so a read-only kit takes it: for a slot of `elements` it sets `slotChipOpenOpt` to `Some` the id, or to `None` when that id is the open one; an id the table lacks leaves the model as it is. (4) `SwapSlot`'s arm (steps 264, 272) also sets `slotChipOpenOpt` to `None` on every outcome, so a pick closes the list whether the swap switched, created or was refused. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 263, 264), whose kit holds the items `LP1`, `QZ`, `Laser`, `LPd` and `QZ2`: `a slot's chip lists the kit's items that fit it`: with a linear polarizer and a sample added, `slotChipItems` of the polarizer's slot is exactly `LP1` and `LPd`, in the order `kitItems` holds them, of the sample's `QZ` and `QZ2`, of the light source's `Laser` and of the seeded detector's none. `ToggleSlotChip opens one chip's list at a time, and a swap closes it`: `ToggleSlotChip` of the sample sets `slotChipOpenOpt` to it, of the polarizer moves it there, and of the polarizer again closes it; `ToggleSlotChip` of an id the table lacks changes nothing; the toggles change no kit file; and with the sample's list open, `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` closes it. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the chip state lands, `model.slotChipItems` MUST list the kit items that fit a slot, `ToggleSlotChip` MUST open one chip's list at a time and close the open one, writing nothing, and `SwapSlot` MUST close the list; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot's chip lists the kit's items that fit it` and `ToggleSlotChip opens one chip's list at a time, and a swap closes it`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.
